# What the galene form, booted as it ships, without a shell and without a
# config, must say on its console (make check-shellfree-galene; test/boot;
# forms/demo/test/console has the format). Galène, given no operator's
# password, parks before galene-setup writes a group or it serves
# anything, and says why; Caddy runs. make check-galene boots it with its
# config, and checks it serves.

seen    galene-needs-config  leash: \{"event":"down","service":"galene","why":"config operator-password: FileNotFound"\}
unseen  caddy-down           leash: \{"event":"down","service":"caddy"
